<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>China's 13-year-old swimming star raises questions on child athletes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97be0297f4fb1226d5b77f63ff0eb074f12a2f7ab90bc17f386c3e3820abc161</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-13-year-old-swimming-star-raises-questions-on-child-athletes/a-79394183--95db71a677f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-13-year-old-swimming-star-raises-questions-on-child-athletes/a-79394183?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three gold medals and three Asian Games records have catapulted China's Yu Zidi, 13, into the sporting spotlight. She is far from the first teen prodigy, but should teens be competing at elite level?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's Vafaei playing for more than snooker glory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a9c0205513e70da5afe982b536565a250f24a4402dc968e457b092b7241538a</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:03Z</updated><published>2026-04-30T13:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-vafaei-playing-for-more-than-snooker-glory/a-76998832--2b4cb996199a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-vafaei-playing-for-more-than-snooker-glory/a-76998832?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years lost to visa battles, Hossein Vafaei is finally delivering on his early promise as a snooker prodigy. He's hoping to inspire people back home amid the turmoil in Iran.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:322bc36b2dcd21ce6925d8bf6e092d4aa4f636232c059f25fc373bc9837e10f0</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Munich and Cologne-Rhine-Ruhr – Germany's two remaining Olympic candidates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2b27af0584b4f76e8036f8c26e2773f0984b1847bb4aeadce266709e131d64f</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-and-cologne-rhine-ruhr-germany-s-two-remaining-olympic-candidates/a-79386915--bae1fd64c3bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-and-cologne-rhine-ruhr-germany-s-two-remaining-olympic-candidates/a-79386915?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Munich or the Cologne-Rhine-Ruhr region? Germany aims to host the Olympic Games again. Just two candidates are left after Berlin pulled out at the last minute.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Could we see MMA at the Olympics?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0fb17c233fe31c230f78ba06aa67dec47d81bf0d274565950d507ee9ca05855</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-we-see-mma-at-the-olympics/a-79369605--f76e8af14c92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-we-see-mma-at-the-olympics/a-79369605?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mixed martial arts has made its debut at the Asian Games this week. It takes the sport closer to the Olympics, but there are doubts about the next step — and the influence of the popular and lucrative UFC.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football in Germany booming, but still much to do</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2202928b8e2b1643db54555bc09c31b9e218f826467d01bd20df918d7a65e88</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T04:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687--313365dcb46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women's football is growing rapidly, particularly in Germany. Nevertheless, equal pay and investment remain major talking points.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>VAR's mission creep a problem for football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c5cbd0ce7cd2017d5b455f6099b97014c7658c6284f74683ce14255e955fb30</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642--644b469bed29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-